{'base__uid': 2743, 'base__ref_base': 'C', 'base__alt_base': 'T', 'base__hugo': 'B3GALT6', 'base__cchange': 'c.*2769C>T', 'base__so': '2KD', 'clinvar__disease_names': None, 'clinvar__id': None, 'dbsnp__rsid': 'rs6603782', 'gnomad__af': 0.460020436837, 'omim__omim_id': None, 'vcfinfo__zygosity': 'het', 'ncbigene__ncbi_desc': 'The enzyme encoded by this intronless gene is a beta-1,3-galactosyltransferase found in the medial Golgi apparatus, where it catalyzes the transfer of galactose from UDP-galactose to substrates containing a terminal beta-linked galactose moiety. The encoded enzyme has a particular affinity for galactose-beta-1,4-xylose found in the linker region of glycosamines. This enzyme is required for glycosaminoglycan synthesis. [provided by RefSeq, Jun 2013]'}
