{'base__uid': 2838, 'base__ref_base': 'T', 'base__alt_base': 'C', 'base__hugo': 'TAS1R3', 'base__cchange': 'c.-1572T>C', 'base__so': '2KU', 'clinvar__disease_names': None, 'clinvar__id': None, 'dbsnp__rsid': 'rs307355', 'gnomad__af': 0.809526846066, 'omim__omim_id': None, 'vcfinfo__zygosity': 'hom', 'ncbigene__ncbi_desc': 'The protein encoded by this gene is a G-protein coupled receptor involved in taste responses. The encoded protein can form a heterodimeric receptor with TAS1R1 to elicit the umami taste response, or it can bind with TAS1R2 to form a receptor for the sweet taste response. [provided by RefSeq, Nov 2015]'}
